<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="section-1" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Dot Product</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      In this section, we will introduce the concept of the dot product, also known as the scalar product, 
      which is an important operation in vector algebra. We will discuss its definition, properties, 
      and applications.
    </p>
  </introduction>
  <objectives>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <p>
            Understand the definition of the dot product and how it is computed for vectors.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Learn the key properties of the dot product, including commutativity, distributivity, and 
            scalar multiplication.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Explore applications of the dot product, such as finding the angle between vectors and 
            determining orthogonality.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
  </objectives>
</section>